meta {
  name: 01 Per-skill practice stays open
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/reading/exercise?modelltest=1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  A START student reaches this. So does a Pro student, a Premium student, and
  an independent one.

  Per-skill practice — `/api/reading`, `/api/listening`, `/api/writing`,
  `/api/sprachbausteine` and speaking practice — is what makes Start a usable
  product rather than a stub. It is deliberately NOT gated on tier.

  (The reading module is served at `/api/reading`; its controller class is
  still called Lesen.)

  Run this with a START student (see `00 How to set a student tier`) and it
  must return 200. If it ever returns 403 TIER_TOO_LOW, the exam gate has
  spread beyond the exam module — and `test/subscription-enforcement.spec.ts`
  should have failed first, since it counts exactly which controllers carry
  the tier guard.

  Try the other skills too. All 200 for Start:

  - `GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listening/teils`
  - `GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sprachbausteine/exercise?modelltest=1`
  - `GET {{baseUrl}}/api/writing/exercise?modelltest=1`

  What a Start student does NOT get is the full timed simulation — that is
  `02 Exam module`.
}
